# VideoBrief — Product

Brand: **VideoBrief** · **Domain:** videobrief.app

**Education-first** personalized YouTube summaries synced with the video. Not a generic AI summarizer. Not a chatbot. Non-educational videos still get a sectioned summary (soft disclaimer, no familiarity question).

## Core loop

Paste URL + familiarity/length sliders (0–100) → stub on library (no redirect) → enqueue analysis job → fetch metadata + EN transcript → classify (`isEducational` + topic) → generate overview + sections **with bodies** → open workspace anytime; watch with sync highlight/seek.

## Guiding question

Does this help turn a YouTube video into a better personalized understanding for this user — especially for learning? If not, keep it out of MVP.

## MVP includes

Landing, auth (email/password + Google), soft email confirm, lightweight **educational** onboarding (YOB, education level, subject chips, optional summary style — all optional), library, YouTube ingest (per-user `user_videos`, re-paste refreshes; fetch **from the analysis worker**), English timestamped captions, AI classify + generate (via `AIProvider`), paste-time familiarity + length sliders (0–100), typed profile prefs, video workspace with overview **summary** + section **bodies** + highlight/seek, soft non-edu disclaimer, dark-default UI, EN-only i18n scaffolding, unit tests, BullMQ analysis worker (Redis queue-only).

## MVP excludes

Chat, uploads, Whisper/audio transcription, non-YouTube, recommendations, knowledge graph, cross-video search, quizzes, social/sharing, Stripe, tRPC, PostHog/analytics, E2E tests, non-English UI or captions, **LLM-invented knowledge questions**, topic/video EAV context, shared cross-user transcript/classification cache. Redis is **queue + per-video lock only** (not a transcript cache).

## UX

Editorial, premium, content-first, typography-led. AI stays invisible in the workspace. Prefer Watch → understand → remember over chat.

## Context rules

- Onboarding stays lightweight; every field optional.
- Profile fields (typed, not open key/value): year of birth (`yyyy`, framing), education-level enum, subject chips (fixed list + `other`), optional `summary_style` (`brief` / `moderate` / `extensive`).
- Per-video prefs live on the **analysis row**, not the profile: familiarity and summary length as integers 0–100 (defaults: familiarity 50; length from `summary_style`). Collected at paste. Re-paste overwrites.
- Non-edu summaries still use profile + length; omit familiarity from the generate prompt; soft disclaimer.
- Ambiguous classification → prefer educational.
- Classify does **not** emit section skeleton or dynamic questions. Generate emits `{ summary, sections: { title, startTime, endTime, body }[] }`.
